==Evolution==
Evolves into '''B.C.S. Lionheart''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''B.C.S. Tigerclaw '''at level 30 by using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

Evolves into '''B.C.S. Beartooth''' at level 60 using [[Catfruit]] and Behemoth Stones.

==Strategy/Usage==
With low movement speed, extremely high attack power, and Massive Damage against [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] and [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] enemies, this unit can be a great aid in battle when fighting them. It also has the ability to stop Zombies from reviving, which makes it a great [[:Category:Zombie Killer Cats|Zombie Killer]] if you can prevent them from burrowing behind it.

High health also allows it to take a few unintended hits and to act as a tank for a short time before being knocked back but typically requires meatshield protection due to the long three minute recharge time. When protected, Lionheart has safe enough standing range for his role, despite the extremely long foreswing. Beware of its long attack animation, as it can easily cause attacks to be interrupted, especially against fast pushers such as [[Bore]], [[Shy Boy]], [[J.K. Bun Bun]] and zombies somehow surfacing within it.

==='''True Form'''===
Having a faster time between attacks means that B.C.S. Tigerclaw gains more DPS and lands attacks more often on the field. Other than that, nothing else changes, but the improvement is very noticeable, making this evolution worth the Catfruits.

==='''Ultra Form'''===
By combining simple but noticeable improvements to its performance, Drednot's ultra form may look basic by a quick glance but it proves to be a destructive force in the battlefield.

Starting by its simplest improvements, the attack and health increase are expected but welcome changes. Though Beartooth may appear to be a specialized unit given its massive damage to red and zombie, the giant battleship has impressive stats for a generalist usage. With its newer buffs it has proven to have an even stronger presence in the battlefield. Sporting an impressive 179k health and 12k dps at level 60, Beartooth serves as a constant and strong force on any enemy that has the misfortune of coming into its range. This allows the war machine to become a solid backliner for common enemies, and a constant nuke for its targets of red and zombie.

And to help with its potential even more, the warship gains some very needed stat buffs beyond its raw power and defense; its range is increased by 40, all the way up to 480, making it an even bigger threat to annoying backliners. While it still gets outranged by [[Zamelle]] and some common red backliners like [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]] and [[Professor A.]], this change allows Beartooth to outrange most midrangers or melee enemies from a safer distance. Its Zombie targetting especially benefits from this, as they tend to be strictly melee attackers.

Additionally to its already improved kit, B.C.S. was blessed with a faster attack speed and animation, allowing its drill which previously came out painfully slow to now hit enemies constantly and furiously. The added speed to its attack was a much needed improvement to the ship, making so that in situations where beforehand it could get its attack interrupted by constant enemy pressure. Now it can exert said pressure back to the enemy field continuously, which is amplified by the range and attack buffs mentioned above.

As a cherry on top, Beartooth also gains knockback immunity. While not a huge improvement in the bigger scheme of things, it makes it so Beartooth can't get its attack interrupted by annoying crowd-control enemies such as [[Red EnerG]] or even [[Trolly Blogger]].

Its recharge time improvement is negligible as the cooldown is still comparatively high to make a huge difference in its versatility.

It is worth mentioning that as a stat based unit, B.C.S. Beartooth gets its usage progressively better with stat buffs, especially coming from level ups. Boosting the unit to level 60 to get its ultra form is not a huge loss in investment, as it pays off in an increasingly stronger and more powerful presence in the battlefield.

However, it's important to point out that Beartooth does not get a new niche, only merely improving on its existing one. If the player is already content with their anti-Zombie and anti-Red counters, or in their midrangers in general, it might be more worthwhile getting Ultra Forms that gain newer niches or that expand your options in the battlefield. This can include [[Mighty Kat-A-Pult (Uber Rare Cat)|Cat-10 Gigapult]] with its Relic targetting, that also improves its own anti-Zombie niche.

==='''Talents'''===
The only real relevant [[Talents|Talent]] that B.C.S. Tigerclaw gains is Dodge Attack; it has a 20% activation chance and a duration of 50 frames (1.67 seconds) at max level. Unfortunately, the low chance makes it unreliable, despite it lasting for 1.67 seconds. Resist Weaken and Resist Freeze are both too situational to be of any relevant use. While the Attack and Health Buff talents are nice, but only recommended to invest in after the unit has been boosted with Catseyes, if even more power is needed. Soulstrike is also mostly useless, as B.C.S Tigerclaw has a very slow attack rate and may end up stuck behind weaker enemies, doing more harm than good.

