==Trivia==
*Prior to [[Version 15.6 Update|Version 15.6]], Mighty Drednot's descriptions stated that it had "huge area damage vs Red and Zombies", which was replaced with "Area attacks deal Massive damage vs. Red and Zombies". The Normal Form's description also did not mention that it targetted Zombies.
**The rewrite in Version 15.6 introduced an error in the Evolved Form's description, where it now says "...the Lionheart Area attacks deal Massive damage..."
***This was corrected in [[Version 15.7 Update|Version 15.7]].
*The B.C.S. Lionheart looks similar to [[wikia:metalslug:Big Shiee|Big Shiee]] of Metal Slug or the Yamato class Battleships.
*The B.C.S. part in its English names may be an acronym for "Battle Cats Ship", much like how U.S.S. stands for "United States Ship" that serve with the U.S. Navy.
*The Evolved Form and True Form names could be a reference to the "Warriors" series written by Erin Hunter, where a character named Lionheart is a deputy and one named Tigerclaw is the antagonist, both of the first series, further supported by the fact that the Warriors characters are almost entirely cats.
*[[Mighty Thermae D-Lux (Uber Rare Cat)|Subterra Sentinels]], B.C.S. Tigerclaw, [[Mighty Bomburr (Uber Rare Cat)|NEK-02 Air Citadel]], [[Mighty Aethur Ltd. (Uber Rare Cat)|Ultra Atlantis Logistix]], [[Mighty Carrowsell (Uber Rare Cat)|Extradimensional Envanz]], and [[Mighty Deth-Troy-R (Uber Rare Cat)|Obliterator Diabolosa]] are the only six units with 6 Talents instead of the usual 5 Talents.
**Incidentally, all six of these units get Soulstrike as one of these Talents.
*In the Japanese Description the Elite Marine Umineko, is the reference of Umineko When They Cry (Japanese: うみねこのなく頃に, Hepburn: Umineko no Naku Koro ni, lit. "When the Seagulls Cry") is a Japanese dōjin soft visual novel series produced by 07th Expansion.

